  "briefMd": "# Phase 4 · Query Routing\n\nThe support bot gets three kinds of questions, and the router already tells you which kind each one is:\n\n- **FAQ**: answered by one short line in the IT help desk FAQ.\n- **Policy**: answered by a policy document, but keyword-stuffed noise documents compete for the top spots.\n- **Procedural**: the answer is a three-step procedure spread over consecutive sentences, so the whole procedure has to sit in one chunk.\n\nSet a separate **top-k / rerank / chunk size** profile for each type. One profile for everything either misses procedures or blows the budget.\n\nThe split is fixed (sentence packing, no overlap); every retrieved chunk is sent to the model in full.\n\n**Gates:** FAQ and procedural recall ≥ 0.85, every policy question answered (recall = 1.00), and mean prompt tokens ≤ 75 on the hidden set.\n",
